sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch03-19> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "A large part of an organism's specific morphology depends on there being, besides an aggregate rate of growth of the whole, a characteristic specific rate of growth for each part or organ, so that small changes in these local rates soon produce striking differences of form.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Each part has its own specific growth rate, on which specific morphology depends";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter III, “The Rate of Growth”; topic “Form as a function of growth rates”. Scope: multicellular organisms"
}
